---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import "../styles/site.css";
import "../styles/legal.css";

// Draft website terms (not the product's subscription terms). Everything in <span class="fill"> is a detail
// the company still has to supply. Have it reviewed by counsel before launch.
const sections = [
  ["about", "About these terms"],
  ["info", "Information on this site"],
  ["examples", "Examples and pictures"],
  ["product", "Using Meridian itself"],
  ["ip", "Our content and name"],
  ["use", "Using this site properly"],
  ["links", "Links to other sites"],
  ["warranty", "No warranty"],
  ["liability", "Limits on our liability"],
  ["law", "Governing law"],
  ["changes", "Changes to these terms"],
  ["contact", "Contact us"],
];
---
<Base
  title="Terms · Meridian"
  description="The terms for using the Meridian website."
  share="og-terms.png"
  shareAlt="Meridian: Website terms of use. The terms' contents, starting with about these terms and information on this site."
>

<main id="main">

<section class="lg-head" id="top"><div class="in">
  <span class="pill">Terms</span>
  <h1>Website terms of use</h1>
  <p class="lead">The terms for using this website. Using Meridian itself is covered by a separate agreement.</p>
  <div class="lg-meta"><span>Last updated: <span class="fill">To fill in: date</span></span><span>Applies to this website</span></div>
  <p class="lg-draft"><b>Draft for review.</b> Highlighted details are still to be filled in, and the text is to be reviewed by counsel before launch.</p>
</div></section>

<section class="lg-body"><div class="in lg-grid">

  <nav class="lg-toc" aria-label="On this page"><details data-phone open>
    <summary><h2>On this page</h2><i class="aplus" aria-hidden="true"></i></summary>
    <ol>{sections.map(([id, label]) => <li><a href={"#" + id}>{label}</a></li>)}</ol>
  </details></nav>

  <div class="lg-doc">

    <section id="about">
      <h2>About these terms</h2>
      <p>This website is run by Venzi Inc., 1460 Broadway, New York, NY 10036, United States ("we", "us"). Meridian is our product. By using it, you agree to these terms. If you don't agree, please don't use the site.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="info">
      <h2>Information on this site</h2>
      <p>This site describes Meridian and how it works. We keep it accurate, but it is general information, not an offer or a contract. Some capabilities are marked <b>Planned</b>: they are on our roadmap and not yet part of the product, and plans can change.</p>
      <p>What Meridian will do for your organization is set out in your agreement with us, not on this site.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="examples">
      <h2>Examples and pictures</h2>
      <p>The people, companies, request numbers and amounts shown on this site are fictional examples. Pictures of the product show how it works; the product you see may differ in detail.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="product">
      <h2>Using Meridian itself</h2>
      <p>Access to the Meridian product is provided under a separate agreement with your organization. That agreement, not these terms, governs your use of the product and the data in it.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="ip">
      <h2>Our content and name</h2>
      <p>The text, design, pictures and code of this site, and the Meridian name and logo, belong to us or the people who license them to us. You may read, share links to and print pages for your own evaluation of Meridian. Please don't copy, change or republish the content otherwise without our written permission.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="use">
      <h2>Using this site properly</h2>
      <p>Please don't:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>try to break, overload or get around the site's security;</li>
        <li>send us false information, or someone else's details without their permission;</li>
        <li>copy the site's content in bulk, or use bots or scrapers to collect it, without our written permission;</li>
        <li>use the site to send spam or anything unlawful.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section id="links">
      <h2>Links to other sites</h2>
      <p>Where we link to other websites, such as the sources cited on the Controls page, we do it for your information. We don't control those sites and aren't responsible for them.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="warranty">
      <h2>No warranty</h2>
      <p>We provide this site "as is". As far as the law allows, we make no promises that it will always be available, error-free or complete.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="liability">
      <h2>Limits on our liability</h2>
      <p>As far as the law allows, we aren't liable for any loss that comes from using this site or relying on its content. Nothing in these terms limits liability that can't be limited by law.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="law">
      <h2>Governing law</h2>
      <p>These terms are governed by the laws of <span class="fill">To fill in: governing law</span>, and the courts of <span class="fill">To fill in: courts</span> have jurisdiction over any dispute about them.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="changes">
      <h2>Changes to these terms</h2>
      <p>We may update these terms. The date at the top shows when they last changed. Using the site after a change means you accept the updated terms.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="contact">
      <h2>Contact us</h2>
      <p>Questions about these terms: <a href="mailto:avneesh@venzi.ai">avneesh@venzi.ai</a>, or write to Venzi Inc., 1460 Broadway, New York, NY 10036, United States. See also our <a href="/privacy">privacy notice</a>.</p>
    </section>

  </div>
</div></section>

</main>
</Base>
